# Lifecycle governance

Follow `AGENTS.md` and `specs/greenfield/INSTRUCTIONS.md` + `ORCHESTRATION_MANIFEST.md` on every chat.

## Gate 2

If `GATE2_APPROVAL.txt` is missing or lacks `[APPROVED: …]`, do not create or edit `backend/pom.xml` or `backend/src/**`. Refuse and ask for approval. Specs, Docker files, and this rule may be edited.

## Stages

Implement only the current stage. Do not skip Gate 3 (schema + encoder + Spring module) before `mvn clean test` in `backend/`. On test failure: fix code, never `@Disabled` / `@Ignore`, max 3 retries, then stop. Do not start Stage 6.

## Lineage

Append `SDLC_AUDIT_LOG.json` and update `SDLC_METRICS.json` per `INSTRUCTIONS.md`. Do not invent coverage or claim generated files in `specs/scenarios/01-greenfield.md`.

## High impact — halt

Changing SQL tables after Gate 2, adding undeclared `backend/pom.xml` dependencies, or dropping the 80% / mandatory test bar requires a new human signature. Re-plan to Stage 1 if `PRD.md` or `SYSTEM_DESIGN.md` changes mid-run.

## Frontend

`specs/frontend/` and `20-frontend-react.mdc` may exist. Do not generate `frontend/src/**` or `frontend/package.json` during the Java stages. The client does not change the OpenAPI contract.
